    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0336" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/>

                <head>No. 156.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 26,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your note of
                    the 12th instant, communicating a proposal in regard to the removal of a remnant
                    of Sitting Bull’s band from Canadian territory to the United States, I have the
                    honor to inform you that the matter is receiving the consideration of this
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
